How do end-users consent to receive messages?
Clients, subcontractors, vendors, and employees opt in at https://constructedmatter.com/sms-opt-in. They enter their name and mobile number, select the separate service/account/project messaging checkbox, and submit "Save My SMS Preferences." The checkbox is optional and unchecked by default. It is separate from marketing consent and other agreements. Users can receive CMI services or use an account without SMS consent. The form identifies Constructed Matter, Inc., describes the messages, and discloses variable frequency, message/data rates, STOP to unsubscribe, and HELP for assistance. Only recipients who select service messaging are enrolled in this campaign; selecting marketing alone does not enroll them. CMI retains the mobile number, consent choice, timestamp, source URL, and disclosure version. Client, subcontractor, or employee status alone does not constitute consent. No purchased or rented contact lists are used. Enrollment for this campaign is through the web form, not an SMS keyword. Privacy Policy: https://constructedmatter.com/privacy-policy Terms and Conditions: https://constructedmatter.com/terms-of-service
